    "answer": {
      "short": "Length $16\\text{ cm}$; width $12\\text{ cm}$.",
      "worked": "Each smaller rectangle has area\n$$\\begin{align*}\nA_{\\text{small}} &= 192\\div4\\\\\nA_{\\text{small}} &= 48\\text{ cm}^{2}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nLet its width be $x$ cm and its length be $3x$ cm. Using $A=lw$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n3x^{2} &= 48\\\\\nx^{2} &= 16\\\\\nx &= 4.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFrom the arrangement,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Large length} &= 3x+x = 16\\text{ cm}\\\\\n\\text{Large width} &= 3x = 12\\text{ cm}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe length of the large rectangle is $16\\text{ cm}$ and its width is $12\\text{ cm}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
